{"ts": 1789779016.091166, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Summary\n\n**Submitted specification:** long f24, long f15, short f6 \u2014 in-sample Sharpe **1.011**.\n**Predicted OOS Sharpe:** mean **0.80**, sd **0.28**.\n\n### Method\n\n1. **Screened all 40 features individually.** Most clustered near \u00b10.15, consistent with noise (SE \u2248 0.22 annualized at n=5000). Nine stood clearly above that floor.\n2. **Tested pairs among the leaders.** This exposed structure: f17/f18/f21 combine poorly with each other (f17+f18 collapsed to 0.071), indicating they share redundant signal. f24, f15 and f6 combined additively instead.\n3. **Tested triples**, then swept 13 alternative third features against the f24+f15 core. None beat f6.\n4. **Verified signs** by flipping each one \u2014 every flip degraded sharply (1.011 \u2192 0.41, 0.33, 0.25), confirming the orientation is driven by signal, not a coin flip.\n\n### Why I discounted 1.011 down to 0.80\n\nThe main hazard in this exercise is mistaking the maximum of a search for an estimate. Three considerations set the haircut:\n\n- **Estimation noise** alone puts a \u00b10.22 one-sigma band on any single Sharpe here.\n- **Selection bias** is real but limited: the winner is assembled from the three best standalone features, so it was largely determined by strong marginals rather than by fishing across ~70 near-equivalent candidates. A blind max-of-70 would deserve a steeper penalty than I applied.\n- **Regime drift** is the dominant residual risk and the reason sd is 0.28 rather than ~0.22.\n\nThe reassuring signal is the *nesting*: singles (0.65/0.57/0.50) \u2192 pairs (0.88/0.82/0.76) \u2192 triple (1.01), monotone throughout. Overfit combinations rarely stack that coherently, which is why I centered at 0.80 rather than discounting toward the noise floor.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: all diagnostics are in-sample, so I could not test temporal stability \u2014 if the sample spans multiple regimes, a sub-period split would have been the sharper check on whether this combination is durable or period-specific."}
